 "id": "stage2_phi_boundary",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "nd_action_correlation"
 ],
 "description": "Stage 2 ('the boundary is destruction') in phi. The agent holds the self's controllable basis (resp_<A>) from the compensated discriminator and rolls the self's bbox forward by it; an action whose rollout leaves the board ([0,h)x[0,w) from the game node) has no modelled continuation = termination (would_die_<A>=1). It then chooses a surviving action. The walls are death understood as a forward-rollout prior, not learned by dying \u2014 no death handler, no threshold tuning. Generated by scripts/gen_stage2_phi_seed.py.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "stage2_phi_boundary",
  "description": "boundary = destruction: an action whose phi-rollout leaves the board ends the self; avoid it."
 },
